    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. following up on that \"any other cause whatsoever\" part—if a tenant tries to argue that a period of total chaos or widespread civil unrest (not specifically listed) qualifies under a broad clause, how much weight do courts actually give to that \"unforeseeability\"? basically, does the sheer randomness of the event help their case?",
